{"title":"Resilient overnight runs: opt-in supervision, durable resume, night-scale budgets, and a real soak gate","objective":"Close the four gaps that keep the confirmed bounded overnight runner from being an unattended service: (1) nothing restarts the run after host/process/network failure, (2) recovery stops at the last durable boundary and never continues automatically (USAGE.md:136), (3) overnight defaults are 120 minutes / 5 sessions (runtime/atl-manager.mjs:417-418), too small for a night, and (4) only unit/API tests exist (verification/overnight_recovery_test.mjs, verification/overnight_host_test.mjs) with no unattended soak evidence against a real provider. Deliver an opt-in supervisor, per-session durable checkpoints with bounded resume, night-scale budgets within existing caps, a documented opt-in OS-scheduler path, and a soak harness (simulated in CI, real-provider opt-in) — without weakening any human gate, the --confirm requirement, or the no-replay rule for in-flight provider sessions.","constraints":["Preserve every trust invariant: explicit --confirm, human gates never bypassed, in-flight provider sessions never replayed (USAGE.md:136; runtime/lib/recovery.mjs HUMAN_ACTION_RE).","Stay inside existing budget validation caps: --max-minutes between 1 and 1440, --max-sessions integer 1-20 (runtime/atl-manager.mjs:419-424); raising overnight defaults must fit these caps or ship an explicit, documented state-contract change.","ATL must not silently install OS scheduled tasks (USAGE.md:136); any scheduler integration is print/review/opt-in only.","Keep the single global run slot and the durable ledger at .trust/manager/overnight/run.json backward-compatible (version the schema if fields are added).","Preserve subscription-auth safety: known API/provider env vars stay stripped from children.","Windows-first host; supervisor must handle sleep/hibernate and network loss as expected events, not exceptions.","Evidence-gated SDD/TDD: every implementation step lands only behind a failing-then-passing verifier; no check is claimed passed in this plan.","Scope is bounded to the stated intent: supervision/resume/budgets/soak — no new product surfaces, no merge/deploy/external-messaging capability."],"risks":[{"risk":"Auto-restart multiplies overnight spend beyond intent","mitigation":"Hard wall-clock and session caps inherited from the budget flags; supervisor counts spent budget across restarts and stops at the cap; morning report lists total sessions/tokens."},{"risk":"Supervisor masks a crashloop by restarting forever","mitigation":"Restart cap (default 3) with backoff; on exhaustion the run is marked failed-supervisor-cap and the supervisor exits."},{"risk":"Resume after process death double-applies task changes","mitigation":"Checkpoint only at completed-session boundaries; an interrupted session stays interrupted and excluded from recovery, exactly as documented today."},{"risk":"OS-scheduler entry point could start a run with no human present","mitigation":"Scheduled command consumes a pre-armed, explicitly confirmed intent file; no scheduling without a prior --confirm; ATL prints the command instead of installing it."},{"risk":"Laptop sleep or network drop mid-soak produces false confidence","mitigation":"Soak harness injects crash and network-drop events deterministically rather than assuming a quiet night."},{"risk":"Real-provider soak is slow, costs money, and flakes CI","mitigation":"CI soak uses a scripted mock provider CLI; the live-provider soak is a separate opt-in command with a small budget, documented but never run by tests."},{"risk":"Budget-cap or schema changes break the lifecycle model or older ledgers","mitigation":"Verification/atl_manager_lifecycle_model.py and a schema-version check are updated in the same step as any contract change."}],"completion_checks":[{"check":"Killing the runner mid-session leaves the ledger marking that session interrupted and recover --confirm continues only untouched tasks, never the interrupted session","evidence":"extended verification/overnight_recovery_test.mjs"},{"check":"Opt-in supervisor relaunches a crashed runner within remaining budget, respects the restart cap with backoff, and records supervisor events in run.json","evidence":"new verification/overnight_supervisor_test.mjs driven by a fake runner that exits nonzero"},{"check":"Night-scale budgets are accepted and enforced: e.g. --max-minutes 480 --max-sessions 18 passes validation, values above 1440 minutes or 20 sessions are rejected, and overnight defaults are night-scale","evidence":"new verification/overnight_budget_test.mjs"},{"check":"Unattended soak completes a multi-session run against the mock provider with an injected crash and network drop, producing a per-session report; every session ends in a known terminal state","evidence":"new verification/overnight_soak_sim_test.mjs"},{"check":"Scheduler output is review-only: printed Task Scheduler command references the pre-armed intent file and nothing is installed as a side effect","evidence":"new verification/overnight_schedule_test.mjs"},{"check":"No regressions to existing overnight/recovery/abort behavior and the lifecycle model still matches the state contract","evidence":"verification/overnight_host_test.mjs, verification/run_abort_test.mjs, verification/recovery_test.mjs, verification/atl_manager_lifecycle_model.py"}],"acceptance_examples":[{"example":"atl overnight 017-task --confirm --max-minutes 480 --max-sessions 18 is accepted; the runner is killed at minute 30 mid-session; atl overnight status shows that session interrupted and untouched tasks pending; atl overnight recover --confirm resumes only untouched tasks and the ledger contains no replayed in-flight session.","expected":"durable boundary behavior identical in kind to today, scaled to night budgets"},{"example":"With --watch, the runner script simulates a crash after session 2; the supervisor relaunches it, the run continues from the last completed-session checkpoint, and a third crash exhausts the restart cap so the run ends failed-supervisor-cap.","expected":"bounded automatic restart with visible supervisor events"},{"example":"Soak simulation: mock provider, 6 sessions, forced network drop after session 2 and one forced crash — the final report lists per-session status, duration, and session counts, and exits 0 only if all sessions reached a terminal state.","expected":"first real unattended soak evidence, deterministic in CI"},{"example":"atl overnight schedule --print emits a Windows Task Scheduler command/XML for review that targets the confirmed intent file; nothing is registered unless the operator runs the printed command themselves.","expected":"scheduler path documented and reviewable without silent installation"}],"selected_skills":["agent-trust-ladder","atl-implement","atl-beacon"],"proposed_worker":"pip","implementation_steps":[{"id":"1","title":"Evidence and spec baseline","detail":"Write .trust/specs/018-resilient-overnight/brief.md and spec capturing the four gaps with citations (USAGE.md:136; runtime/atl-manager.mjs:417-424; verification/overnight_recovery_test.mjs; verification/overnight_host_test.mjs) and the acceptance examples above. No code changes in this step.","files":[".trust/specs/018-resilient-overnight/brief.md",".trust/specs/018-resilient-overnight/spec.md"],"gate":"spec files exist and cite the evidence; no runtime file touched"},{"id":"2","title":"Night-scale budgets (TDD)","detail":"Add failing verification/overnight_budget_test.mjs first: overnight defaults become night-scale (e.g. 480 minutes / 18 sessions, both within the existing 1440/20 caps), flags above caps still rejected. Then adjust parseWorkerFlags in runtime/atl-manager.mjs. Any cap change is recorded as an explicit contract change, not a silent raise.","files":["runtime/atl-manager.mjs","verification/overnight_budget_test.mjs"],"gate":"overnight_budget_test.mjs exits 0 and existing flag validation tests still hold"},{"id":"3","title":"Durable per-session checkpoints and bounded resume","detail":"Extract overnight ledger handling into runtime/lib/overnight.mjs; record one checkpoint per session (sessionId, taskId cursor, status, startedAt/endedAt, budget spent) in .trust/manager/overnight/run.json with a schema version; recovery continues only from the last completed-session boundary and keeps interrupted sessions excluded. Extend verification/overnight_recovery_test.mjs with kill-mid-session cases before implementing.","files":["runtime/lib/overnight.mjs","runtime/atl-manager.mjs","verification/overnight_recovery_test.mjs"],"gate":"extended overnight_recovery_test.mjs exits 0 including the new kill/resume cases"},{"id":"4","title":"Opt-in supervisor with restart cap","detail":"Add runtime/lib/supervisor.mjs and an atl overnight --watch mode: spawn the runner, restart on nonzero exit while wall-clock/session budget remains, cap restarts (default 3) with backoff, mark failed-supervisor-cap on exhaustion, and append supervisor events to the ledger. Cover with verification/overnight_supervisor_test.mjs using a fake runner script that crashes on cue; include a simulated sleep/wake clock jump.","files":["runtime/lib/supervisor.mjs","runtime/atl-manager.mjs","verification/overnight_supervisor_test.mjs"],"gate":"overnight_supervisor_test.mjs exits 0 covering restart, backoff, cap exhaustion, and budget stop"},{"id":"5","title":"Review-only OS scheduler path","detail":"Add atl overnight schedule --print emitting a Windows Task Scheduler command/XML that runs the supervisor against a pre-armed, previously confirmed intent file; ATL itself never registers the task. Document in USAGE.md (overnight paragraph near line 136), runtime/README.md, and docs/reference.html. Cover with verification/overnight_schedule_test.mjs asserting print-only behavior and intent-file requirement.","files":["runtime/atl-manager.mjs","runtime/lib/overnight.mjs","USAGE.md","runtime/README.md","docs/reference.html","verification/overnight_schedule_test.mjs"],"gate":"overnight_schedule_test.mjs exits 0; docs updated with the still-open-AI-session constraint stated plainly"},{"id":"6","title":"Soak harness: simulated in CI, live opt-in","detail":"Add verification/overnight_soak_sim_test.mjs driving >=6 sessions against a scripted mock provider CLI with an injected crash and a forced network drop, asserting every session reaches a terminal state and the report (per-session status, durations, budget) is written for atl overnight status. Add a separate documented opt-in live-provider soak command with a small fixed budget that tests never invoke automatically.","files":["verification/overnight_soak_sim_test.mjs","verification/mocks/mock-provider.mjs","runtime/atl-manager.mjs","docs/reference.html"],"gate":"overnight_soak_sim_test.mjs exits 0 deterministically; live soak documented as manual-only"},{"id":"7","title":"Lifecycle model and docs reconciliation","detail":"Update verification/atl_manager_lifecycle_model.py to model supervisor and checkpoint states consistently with the state contract (config/manager-state-contract.json), refresh docs/control-room.html / docs/reference.html overnight sections, and record the final behavior in the spec's verify notes.","files":["verification/atl_manager_lifecycle_model.py","config/manager-state-contract.json","docs/control-room.html","docs/reference.html",".trust/specs/018-resilient-overnight/spec.md"],"gate":"lifecycle model runs and matches the updated contract; docs and spec agree with implementation"}],"verifier_commands":["node verification/overnight_budget_test.mjs","node verification/overnight_recovery_test.mjs","node verification/overnight_supervisor_test.mjs","node verification/overnight_schedule_test.mjs","node verification/overnight_soak_sim_test.mjs","node verification/overnight_host_test.mjs","node verification/run_abort_test.mjs","node verification/recovery_test.mjs","python -I verification/atl_manager_lifecycle_model.py"]}
